(vector (map (:adr/authoritative_for (vector "new repo kotoba-lang/i18n: portable .cljc i18n library (message registry, defmessages compile-time accessors, CLDR-lite plural rules, RTL/tier language registry, etzhayyim TM-service JSON bridge, shitsuke-seam re-frame/reagent integration)" "i18n.core/plural/registry/messages/tm-import are zero third-party runtime deps (mirrors dot/jsonlogic/toml); only i18n.re-frame/i18n.reagent depend on shitsuke" "defmessages macro is the paraglide-js equivalent for cljc: reads an EDN catalog at macroexpansion time, emits one defn per key calling i18n.core/t (key set fixed at compile time, translated text stays a runtime lookup so set-locale! needs no rebuild)" "select-map plural/gender branching ({:select :count :one ... :other ...}) is Fluent-inspired, mirroring what paraglide v2's own match/when syntax already borrows from Project Fluent" "i18n.tm-import is a pure data-shape bridge (flat dotted-key JSON <-> namespaced-keyword catalog; GetLanguageRegistry response -> i18n.registry/load! entries) with no HTTP client of its own — i18n.etzhayyim.com stays the system of record for LLM translation + human-approval QA" "i18n.reagent/locale-links + wire-lang-switch! generalize the delegated a[data-lang] click-listener pattern already proven by kami-mangaka-reader/src/kami/mangaka/reader/app.cljs" "i18n.messages/embed-catalog (added post-acceptance): reads an EDN catalog at macroexpansion time and inlines it as a literal map — the cljs bootstrap counterpart to defmessages, since ClojureScript has no runtime classpath resource loading to feed i18n.core/register! from a browser build" "ClojureScript consumers of defmessages/embed-catalog MUST :require i18n.messages with :include-macros true — plain :refer fails to resolve the macro under cljs at all, and bare :require-macros compiles but leaves macro-generated i18n.core/t calls unresolved under :advanced optimization (found via app-aozora integration, PR gftdcojp/app-aozora#46)")), (:adr/supersedes (vector)), (:adr/superseded_by (vector)), (:adr/topic "kotoba-lang-i18n-design"), (:adr/related (vector)), (:adr/status "accepted"), (:adr/id "adr-2607051210-kotoba-lang-i18n-design"), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:adr/last_verified "2026-07-05"), (:adr/body "# ADR-2607051210: kotoba-lang/i18n — portable cljc i18n library\n\n**Status**: accepted (implemented, closed out)\n**Date**: 2026-07-04 (follow-up/close-out: 2026-07-05)\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki\n\nSee the companion .md file in this same directory for the full context,\ndecision, consequences, and follow-up/close-out sections (identical body,\nkept in sync)."), (:adr/deciders (vector "Jun Kawasaki")), (:adr/artifacts "{:i18n \"kotoba-lang/i18n @ ac3eb3313ca4e60ce3167a9188751568a4df7e00 (37 tests/85 assertions, 0 failures, JVM — clojure -M:test with real git-pinned shitsuke dep, matches CI; adds embed-catalog + :include-macros true docs over the initial d31ea59 acceptance commit)\", :app-aozora \"gftdcojp/app-aozora PR #46 (open, not merged) — first real consumer: shell + settings/home/feeds/credits pages migrated to defmessages accessors, ja source + en translation, header locale switcher; verified via scratch shadow-cljs :advanced build, 0 warnings\"}"), (:adr/date "2026-07-04"), (:db/id -1), (:adr/authoritative true), (:adr/title "ADR-2607051210: kotoba-lang/i18n — portable cljc i18n library"), (:adr/source-format "edn")))